=== SIGNATURE ===
z_change_counts(best, du, vstar, ncoins)

=== COMMENT ===
Private helper for make_change - do not call directly. Backtracks the min-coins table from amount vstar to 0, tallying how many of each of the ncoins denominations were used. Returns a 1-by-ncoins row of counts.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(best, du, vstar, ncoins, LET(
   inf, 1000000000,
   alen, ROWS(best),
   seq, SEQUENCE(alen, 1, 0),
   seqc, SEQUENCE(ncoins, 1, 1),
   seqr, SEQUENCE(1, ncoins),
   kmin, SUM(best * (seq = vstar)),
   zeros, SEQUENCE(1, ncoins, 0, 0),
   IF(OR(vstar <= 0, kmin <= 0, kmin >= inf),
      zeros,
      DROP(
         REDUCE(HSTACK(vstar, zeros), SEQUENCE(kmin), LAMBDA(acc, step, LET(
            rem, INDEX(acc, 1, 1),
            cnt, DROP(acc, , 1),
            bestrem, SUM(best * (seq = rem)),
            prevb, MAP(du, LAMBDA(coin, IF((coin >= 1) * (coin <= rem), SUM(best * (seq = (rem - coin))), inf))),
            pick, (du >= 1) * (prevb = bestrem - 1),
            hit, XMATCH(1, pick),
            chosen, SUM(du * (seqc = hit)),
            HSTACK(rem - chosen, cnt + (seqr = hit))
         ))),
         , 1
      )
   )
))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Private helper for make_change. Reconstructs the per-denomination coin counts from the DP table produced by z_change_costs.

Arguments:
  best   - the min-coins-per-amount column from z_change_costs.
  du     - the denominations in integer GCD units (0 = unusable), aligned to the original coins order.
  vstar  - the chosen target amount (largest reachable value not exceeding the price).
  ncoins - the number of denominations (rows) to report.

Returns:
  A 1-by-ncoins row giving how many of each denomination make up vstar with the fewest coins. Each step picks a denomination that lies on an optimal (one-coin-cheaper) path and subtracts it until the amount reaches 0. Returns all zeros when vstar is 0 or unreachable.

Implementation note: it reads best[k] as SUM(best*(seq=k)) and du[hit] as SUM(du*(seqc=hit)) rather than INDEX(best, ...)/INDEX(du, ...). Excel mis-evaluates INDEX into these computed arrays (which come from a REDUCE and, via make_change, from a range) when several make_change calls share a sheet - it silently collapses the answer to a single coin. Element-wise selection with SUM (and MAP for the per-coin lookups) is evaluated reliably.

Called only by make_change; not intended for direct worksheet use.
